From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: akramboussanni <92455979+akramboussanni@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 19 Nov 2026 17:20:17 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] gnome: Connect with the link from Kimono Prayer

Why: the extension reads everything through a person's own Kimono Prayer link
(https://<kimono>/api/v1/prayer/feed/<token>), which stands in for signing in.
Until it has one it can't do anything, so it asks for it.

What must survive upstream changes:
- kimono.js (no imports, so node can test it) has kimonoLink(): it accepts the
  bare link or mawaqit-kimono://connect?link=<urlencoded link>, only http(s)
  with the path /api/v1/prayer/feed/<token>, and drops any query.
- The search entry is where the link is pasted: not connected, its hint says
  "Paste your Kimono Prayer link", the location button and calculated menu are
  hidden, and the status asks for the link. Submitting anything else repeats it.
- The link is state.link in ~/.config/kimono-prayer/state.json (written with
  Gio.FileCreateFlags.PRIVATE, as upstream saves its state).
- Connecting replaces any saved place and calendar (keeping the notification
  and icon-only switches) and loads at once. "Disconnect from Kimono", shown
  while connected, forgets the link and the times.
- tests/kimono.mjs covers the parser (node tests/kimono.mjs).

diff --git a/gnome/mawaqit@akramb.com/extension.js b/gnome/mawaqit@akramb.com/extension.js
